{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=2d553b38-80a2-5c94-cf4e-eb42dbf70b91": {
      "title": "Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Director of Student Engagement Apply Share Link copied Position: Director of Student Engagement Status: Regular, Full-time, Exempt Department: Student Life Reports to: Dean of Student Life Compensation: $85,000.00 - $90,000.00 annual salary Description: The Director of Student Engagement provides strategic leadership for programs and initiatives that strengthen student belonging, well-being, persistence, and success at Paul Smith’s College. Guided by the College’s experiential learning model and hands-on philosophy, this role designs, implements, and assesses a comprehensive student engagement framework that extends across the student experience and supports institutional retention and student success goals. As a senior member of the Student Life leadership team, the Director works closely with the Dean of Student Life to advance departmental priorities, coordinate selected cross-functional initiatives, and respond to emerging student needs. The Director collaborates with colleagues across the institution to develop and execute student-focused strategies in support of the College’s strategic plan, and uses data and analytics to measure impact and guide continuous improvement. This role is a key member of the Enrollment and Experience Council. Duties & Responsibilities: Leadership & Supervision Provide strategic and day-to-day leadership for a campus-wide approach to student engagement that fosters inclusion, belonging, well-being, and persistence from enrollment through graduation. Supervise professional and student staff, manage budgets and resources, and ensure efficient, mission-aligned operations across the Student Engagement portfolio. Oversee hiring, training, and evaluation of staff and student employees within the Office of Student Engagement. Contribute to departmental strategic planning, priority setting, assessment, and planning for future growth. Coordinate implementation of selected department-wide priorities, establishing timelines, clarifying responsibilities, tracking progress, and keeping the Dean informed of emerging issues. Student Engagement Direct the development and implementation of an annual calendar of student programs consistent with the strategic plan of both the Department of Student Life and the College overall. Program development will touch on social, recreational and cultural themes and include program design, implementation and evaluation. Provide primary staff supervision for all registered student clubs and student-led organizations to ensure compliance with college guidelines and assist in creating strategies to enhance their visibility. Serve as the primary advisor to the Student Government Association, guiding student leaders in building effective governance structures, advocacy initiatives, and cross-campus collaborations that promote involvement and amplify the student voice. Assess the effectiveness of engagement programs and broader student experience initiatives; compile and analyze data for reports, identify trends and gaps, and work with colleagues to improve services and outcomes for students. Collaboration Collaborate with colleagues within Student Life and across the College to support integrated student success strategies, including Living Learning Communities and other cross-functional programs and initiatives. Lead or work collaboratively with counterparts to coordinate major cross-functional initiatives, including New Student Orientation, Welcome Week, Open House, and other priorities designated by the Dean of Student Life. Convene and facilitate cross-functional teams when needed to address issues that span multiple areas of the student experience. Serve on the Enrollment and Experience Council and other committees or working groups as assigned, contributing to institutional strategies for student persistence and graduation. Work closely with the Dean of Student Life and maintain strong communication with the Dean of Curriculum to coordinate priorities across academic and Student Life domains. Represent the Department of Student Life in meetings and initiatives as designated by the Dean. Compliance & Risk Management Ensure compliance with institutional policies and applicable regulations related to student life, health, and safety. Promote a safe, inclusive, and supportive campus environment. Budget & Resource Management Support coordinated planning across Student Life by reviewing relevant budgets, identifying shared resource needs, and providing guidance on effective allocation. Identify and support opportunities for grants, partnerships, and external funding that enhance student services and advance departmental priorities. Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs or related field required. Minimum of 5 years of progressive experience in Student Engagement, Campus Activities or Student Affairs Proven success advising student organizations and/or student government bodies. Demonstrated ability to apply and utilize analytics to evaluate engagement and inform program strategy. Demonstrated ability to supervise diverse teams and manage complex programs. Strong understanding of student development theory, engagement strategies, and retention practices. Commitment to inclusive, community-based, and experiential education. Excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Demonstration of leadership skills and ability to build effective professional collaborative working relationships across departments and with external partners. Enthusiasm and skilled at working with diverse student populations. Ability to work with a broad range of diverse individuals and groups to form a safe and inclusive workplace. Ability to navigate complex challenges and demonstrate sharp problem-solution skills by analyzing situations, determining next steps, and implementing solutions. Demonstrated skill in effectively organizing work, files, records, etc., to maintain efficient workflow and robust processes. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written. Strong computer skills and ability to use varied data sources and current Microsoft Office Suite. Present themselves outside the College in a manner in keeping with the College’s core values This position will require evening and weekend work as needed throughout the academic year. Physical Requirements: Environmental Conditions? Work is consistently performed in an indoor office setting with normal temperature ranges for the season.??? Traditional noise of a busy office setting can be expected.?? Lifting and Carrying Ability to regularly lift up to 10 lbs. Frequent lifting and carrying of light to moderate office equipment (laptop or meeting materials) weight items.? Mobility Prolonged sitting majority of the workday to complete responsibilities.?? Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel?to pick up items as necessary. Climbing various staircases across the campus to engage in meetings and/or presentations.?? Dexterity and Hand-Eye Coordination Manual dexterity for handling small office-related objects.? Fine motor skills for work performed on laptop. Infrequent need to reach overhead or below knee level to perform work duties.? Sensory Requirements Good vision, including color vision, with corrective lenses as necessary. ?? Good hearing with assistive devices as necessary. ?? Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. We are reviewing candidates immediately and expect this search to move quickly! Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 60° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Campus Community The Adirondacks Safety & Support Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
    },
    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=31bfe259-7815-a81c-fffc-ca0d71f0ffe8": {
      "title": "Visitor Experience Specialist",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Visitor Experience Specialist Apply Share Link copied Position: Visitor Experience Specialist Status: Full-time, Seasonal, Non-Exempt (Dec – March) Department: Visitor Interpretive Center (VIC) Reports to: General Manager Salary: $19.00/hour Position Description: The Visitor Experience Specialist position provides customer service to the public on the VIC, its trails and history, the surrounding region and Paul Smith’s College. In addition, the position is responsible for retail sales, center maintenance, patrolling the trails to orient visitors to the site, its natural history, and ecology, and supporting other needs of the center. Duties & Responsibilities: Provide excellent customer service to all guests providing information on trail conditions, natural history, center programs, excursions in the surrounding area, and details about Paul Smith’s College. Staff the front desk of the VIC for assigned shifts (½-full day) as the primary point of contact for visitors, both in person and telephone. Manage in person, web-based, and telephone program registrations. Assist with retail sales, managing inventory and restocking. Assist the public with ski and snowshoe rentals. Assist with administrative, maintenance, and logistical needs of the center including maintaining cleanliness of front desk, visitor areas, restrooms and minor maintenance tasks as needed. Patrol trails to orient visitors to the site, check ski passes, enforce center rules and minor trail maintenance. Assist with program and event logistics as needed. Qualifications: All education and experience levels are considered. Knowledge of or interest in Adirondack natural history and ecology. Strong desire to learn, share, and teach about the Adirondacks. Work experience in a related field, including one year of experience with retail sales (operation of cash register) and inventory management preferred. Experience and interest in working with diverse audiences of all ages. Excellent communication skills, including public speaking, over the phone, in person, and written communication. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office, particularly Word and Excel, and point-of-sale systems. Ability to work weekends and events. Reliable transportation to and from work. Ability to work with a broad range of diverse individuals and groups to form a safe and inclusive workplace. Preferred: Certification in at least one of the following or willingness to obtain: First aid/CPR, Wilderness First Aid, or Wilderness First Responder. Physical Requirements: Environmental Conditions Perform moderate physical tasks outdoors in all seasons and weather. Ability to comfortably transition from an indoors, climate-controlled environment to potentially inclement weather outdoors multiple times throughout the day. Lifting and Carrying Ability to regularly lift items up to 50 lbs. alone and heavier with assistance. Frequent lifting and carrying moderate to heavy items including furniture, construction materials, and large tools. Mobility Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel?to pick up items as necessary. Climbing various staircases across the campus to engage in meetings and/or presentations. Capable of walking unassisted on uneven surfaces 1-3 miles per day. Ability to hike/snowshoe several miles on gentle, rolling hiking trails with a mix of terrain including roots, rocks, boardwalks. Utilize mobility assistive devices and equipment as necessary. Prolonged periods of standing, walking, and moving to complete daily tasks. Ability to hike/snowshoe several miles on gentle, rolling hiking trails with a mix of terrain including roots, rocks, boardwalks. Ability to climb ladders. Ability to enter and exit a UTV, ATV, and snowmobile frequently throughout the day. Ability to shovel snow in winter. Dexterity and Hand-Eye Coordination Manual dexterity for operating hand and power tools. Fine motor skills for work performed on laptop. Frequent need to reach overhead or below shoulder level to perform work duties. Sensory Requirements Good vision, with corrective lenses as necessary. Good hearing with assistive devices as necessary. Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Application review starts immediately with expected start date of December 1, 2026 Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 60° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Campus Community The Adirondacks Safety & Support Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
    },
    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=0a4541b8-b4ed-73d4-9b2c-42a63a8be27d": {
      "title": "Winter Ski Trail Groomer",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Winter Ski Trail Groomer Apply Share Link copied Position : Winter Ski Trail Groomer Status: Temporary/ Seasonal, Non-exempt, ON CALL Department: Visitor’s Interpretive Center (VIC) Reports to: Trails and Facilities Manager Salary: $22.00/hour Description: The Winter Trail Groomer position maintains and grooms 25 miles of trails for various winter activities, including recreational and competitive skiing and snowshoeing. The primary duties are operating and maintaining grooming equipment (snowmobiles, snow cats, etc.). Work hours will include weekends and night shifts. Flexibility in scheduling is essential, as work hours will vary depending on weather conditions and event needs. Duties & Responsibilities: Prepare groomed trail surfaces for a variety of configurations and uses including recreational and competitive events for skate, classic cross-country skiing and snowshoeing. Operate grooming equipment safely and efficiently including tracked ATV’s and UTV’s, snowmobiles, drag and roller equipment, and a snow cat (Piston Bully 100) with dual track setters and a 12-way blade. Perform routine, daily maintenance checks on equipment prior to utilization. Conduct necessary repairs to equipment as needed to ensure safe and reliable equipment, and a well-maintained trail system. Operate power saw and hand tools to improve trails including the use of chainsaws, pole saws, and snow shovels. Collaborate with college staff and others to plan and implement winter trail races and events Implement daily, seasonal, short and long-term maintenance plans in coordination with supervisor for equipment, tools, snow cat barn, and trail infrastructure. Coordinate with supervisor for budgeting and purchasing tools, equipment, fluids, and maintenance items for equipment. Daily inspection of trail system mitigating safety and comfort concerns including trail surface and tree management. Assessment and repair including shoveling trailside benches and stocking trailside outhouses. Installation and monitoring of trail wayfinding signage and race signage as needed. Manage the on-site needs of the grooming operation including general upkeep of workspace, fuel and fluids, signage, and providing a published daily grooming report. Qualifications: Demonstrated experience in operating heavy equipment. Demonstrated knowledge of Nordic skiing, its various disciplines, and the varieties of groomed terrain that support it. Desire and ability to operate power saw and hand tools to improve trails including the use of chainsaws, pole saws, and snow shovels. Knowledge of and desire to maintain safety at the workplace regarding power tools, heavy equipment, and risk in the outdoor winter environment. Ability to work weekends, holidays, irregular hours, and evening work a must. Ability to work with a broad range of diverse individuals and groups to form a safe and inclusive workplace. Preferred: 2-years’ experience operating and maintaining Nordic ski grooming equipment including a Piston Bully 100, snowmobiles, ATV, and UTV’s. Proficiency in preparation of groomed trail surfaces for a variety of configurations and uses including recreational and competitive events for skate, classic cross-country skiing and snowshoeing. Demonstrated knowledge of event preparation including placement of appropriate signage, V-Boards, flagging and grooming to produce desired race configurations. Preferably certified in, or willing to obtain the following certifications: Wilderness First Responder, CPR and First Aid, valid driver’s license, chainsaw safety certifications, heavy equipment operator certifications. Physical Requirements: Environmental Conditions? The Work of this position is primarily performed outdoors. Seasonal temperatures should be expected and various noise levels dependent on equipment being used to perform job duties should be expected. Lifting and Carrying Occasionally lifting and carrying of equipment weighing 50 lbs. Equipment and related debris are of various shapes and sizes so may require unusual gripping points. Mobility Occasional standing and walking across snow covered surfaces potentially utilizing snowshoes. Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel to pick up items, as necessary. May have to climb some moderately challenging steep hills and hike up to two miles. Frequent need to reach overhead or below waist level to perform work duties. Dexterity and Hand-Eye Coordination Manual dexterity for handling tools and equipment used in the performance of duties. Sensory Requirements Good vision, including color vision, with corrective lenses as necessary. ?? Good hearing with assistive devices as necessary. ?? Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Review of candidates starts immediately! Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 60° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Campus Community The Adirondacks Safety & Support Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
