    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=b825c392-6e10-6d74-e38e-4aeb0db6ab4f": {
      "title": "Dean of Work",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Dean of Work Apply Share Link copied Position: Dean of Work Status: Regular, Full-time, Exempt Department: Office of the President Reports to: President Salary: $90,000.00 - $110,000 annually Why Paul Smith’s College? Paul Smith’s College has been producing work-ready graduates with sharp minds and calloused hands for over 80 years. Located in the heart of New York’s six-million-acre Adirondack Park, the College offers hands-on learning in fields such as environmental studies, forestry, hospitality, culinary arts, natural sciences, and sustainability. Paul Smith’s College is dedicated to preparing students for leadership in meaningful careers, creating sustainable communities, and fostering a resilient planet. Its immersive, experiential approach blends academic rigor with real-world application in one of the most beautiful, inspiring, and ecologically rich regions in the country. Position Overview The Dean of Work at Paul Smith's College directs a comprehensive Work Experience Program, aligning campus employment with hands-on academic curricula. This is a newly created position in response to the recently expanded Work Experience Program at Paul Smith’s College. This 12-month administrator will manage campus-wide work placements, evaluate student and work crew performance, and partner with a variety of campus operations and institutes. The Dean of Work provides strategic and operational leadership for all student labor and experiential work programs across the college's 13,000-acre Adirondack campus. This role ensures that student employment serves as a vital co-curricular touchstone, fostering work ethic, professional competency, and financial self-reliance. This cabinet-level position reports directly to the Office of the President. Key Responsibilities: Program Strategy & Development: Design and scale a unified student work program blending operational campus needs (e.g., forestry, culinary, hospitality, and research) with intentional learning outcomes. The program design will follow Federal Work College regulations. Operations & Placement: Oversee placement, tracking, and evaluation of student workers in partnership with campus work crew supervisors. Assessment: Monitor student labor performance and retention impact. Oversee the development and implementation of a student Work Transcript. Budget & Compliance: Manage student employment budgets, and adherence to federal/state labor standards. Community Partnerships: Cultivate internal and external partnerships to expand meaningful micro-credentialing and hands-on skill acquisition. Enterprise Development: Develop external-facing student enterprises in collaboration with the Office of Strategic Initiatives. Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Business Management, Student Affairs, or related field (Doctorate preferred). Experience: Minimum 7–10 years of progressive leadership in higher education, experiential education, or operational management. The ideal candidate would have prior experience at a federally recognized Work College. Skills: Strong understanding of student development theory, labor management, budget oversight, and small-campus operations. Attributes: Deep appreciation for hands-on, place-based education within a rural, residential forest setting. Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Review of applicants starts immediately! Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 60° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Campus Community The Adirondacks Safety & Support Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans The Adirondacks Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
